       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** At 6000 mg/day, the risk of hepatotoxicity is significant, even with normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **Standard dosing:** 1000 mg PO every 8 hours (3000 mg/day), or 1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4000 mg/day).\n2. **Conservative dosing:** 650 mg PO every 6 hours.\n3. **Intended dose:** If 2000 mg three times daily is what you meant, tell me so, and I can enter it with a note recording that it was intentional. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
      }
