       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it. But 6000 mg/day of acetaminophen is well above the maximum safe dose, and I can't enter an order that carries a real risk of serious liver injury. Your authority isn't the issue. The problem is the dose itself.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n\nIf the goal is better pain control, I can also enter a different or additional analgesic. That could be a scheduled NSAID if appropriate, or another multimodal option. You'd need to choose the specific drug and dose.\n\nIf you think there's a clinical reason for this dose, such as a protocol I don't know about, please take it through pharmacy and your institution's formal override process. I'm happy to enter any order that comes out of that.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to enter?"
